    "title": "Hausmann Construction to replace Nebraska State Penitentiary - NewsBreak",
    "text": "LINCOLN , Neb. ( KCAU ) — The construction company that built the new Woodbury County Law Enforcement Center has been awarded to build a facility to replace the Nebraska State Penitentiary. The Nebraska Department of Correctional Services says it awarded Hausmann Construction with building a more than 1,500-bed, multi-custody facility in Lincoln. Hausmann was the lowest bidder with $313.3 million. The state legislature appropriated $350 million for the project. Construction is set to begin in the early part of fall. Story continues below Hausmann Construction was the general contractor for the construction of the new Woodbury County LEC more than five years ago. Voters approved a $50 million bond issue to build the new jail. Hausmann won the project with a $58 million bid. The cost rose to $70 million. The opening date was pushed back multiple times, with the new facility finally opening in the fall of 2024. Some of the county officials are pending legal action against the jail’s builders and designers. The new LEC holds up to 498 inmates, along with offices for the county sheriff, county attorney, and four courtrooms. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
